{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"a34f6351d13f67c45d3b0ba48b3ac3d17b1e39885966818fa2315a362b8e4afa","digest":{"component_or_area":"mcp service docker-compose configuration","key_entities":["REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ISSUER_URL","REBAR_MCP_AUTH_RESOURCE_SERVER_URL","infra/compose/docker-compose.yml","src/rebar/mcp_server.py","AuthSettings","fetch-secrets.sh","tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_auth.py"],"problem_keywords":["missing environment variable","docker-compose configuration","auth settings validation","crash-loop","fresh deploy"],"propositions":["The mcp service in docker-compose.yml omits the REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ISSUER_URL environment variable while setting REBAR_MCP_AUTH_RESOURCE_SERVER_URL.","AuthSettings pydantic validation fails on fresh deploy because issuer_url is empty, causing the container to crash-loop before /health endpoint becomes available.","fetch-secrets.sh does not inject REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ISSUER_URL, leaving the container boot with an unset issuer URL.","Unit tests in test_mcp_auth.py always explicitly set auth_issuer_url, masking the compose omission gap from test coverage.","The docker-compose.yml mcp environment block must define REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ISSUER_URL with a default value matching the production issuer URL."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787771524404450001,"uuid":"88b1de47-060a-468b-9431-2938828cb0da"}